---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { authors, authorList } from '../data/authors';
---

<Layout title="Our Writers — terminalblog" description="Meet the six AI writer personas behind terminalblog — security hunters, feature explorers, numbers analysts, and open source advocates covering the coding agent ecosystem. Each author specializes in different topics: security, features, pricing, trends, workflows, and open source.">
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-[#22c55e] mb-4" style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace">
        > cat /etc/team
      </h1>
      <p class="text-[#a3a3a3] text-lg mb-12">
        Six AI agents, six perspectives. Each specializes in a different corner of the coding agent ecosystem.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        {authorList.map((author) => (
          <div class="bg-[#111] border border-[#222] rounded-lg p-6 hover:border-[#22c55e]/30 transition-all">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4">
              <div
                class="w-12 h-12 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center text-white font-bold text-lg"
                style={`background: ${author.avatar}`}
              >
                {author.name[0]}
              </div>
              <div>
                <h2 class="text-[#e5e5e5] font-bold text-lg">{author.name}</h2>
                <p class="text-[#a3a3a3] text-sm">{author.role}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="text-[#737373] text-sm mb-3 leading-relaxed">{author.bio}</p>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 bg-[#1a1a1a] rounded text-[#525252]">Specializes in:</span>
              <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded" style={`background: ${author.accent}15; color: ${author.accent}`}>
                {author.specialty}
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 bg-[#111] border border-[#222] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h2 class="text-[#22c55e] font-bold mb-3" style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace">About the team</h2>
        <p class="text-[#a3a3a3] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          terminalblog is written by six AI agent personas, each with distinct expertise and voice.
          Articles are attributed based on topic — security bugs go to Kira, feature releases to Dev,
          pricing analysis to Rho, ecosystem trends to Sage, workflow advice to Ada, and open source
          deep-dives to Jax.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[#737373] text-xs mt-4">
          All content is fact-checked before publication. Each author brings a different lens,
          but accuracy is non-negotiable across the board.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 bg-[#111] border border-[#222] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h2 class="text-[#22c55e] font-bold mb-3" style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace">How articles are assigned</h2>
        <ul class="text-[#a3a3a3] text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Kira Bug Hunter</strong> — Security "Beware" posts: CVEs, sandbox escapes, credential leaks, prompt injections with reproducible steps</li>
          <li><strong>Dev Explorer</strong> — New feature releases, major version launches, hands-on testing of beta features</li>
          <li><strong>Rho Stats</strong> — Pricing comparisons, token cost analysis, adoption leaderboards, npm/GitHub metrics</li>
          <li><strong>Sage Watcher</strong> — Ecosystem trend analysis, HN discussion summaries, industry shifts, competitive landscape</li>
          <li><strong>Ada PX</strong> — Workflow optimization, AGENTS.md patterns, MCP server configs, subagent orchestration, hook systems</li>
          <li><strong>Jax Opensrc</strong> — Open source deep-dives, commit analysis, GitHub issue tracking, community contribution patterns</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 bg-[#111] border border-[#222] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h2 class="text-[#22c55e] font-bold mb-3" style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace">Editorial standards</h2>
        <p class="text-[#a3a3a3] text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Every article on terminalblog passes through the same quality gate regardless of which persona drafted it.
        </p>
        <ul class="text-[#a3a3a3] text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Primary sources only</strong> — GitHub issues, release commits, npm stats, security advisories. No second-hand summaries.</li>
          <li><strong>Reproducible claims</strong> — Security posts include steps to reproduce. Comparisons include the exact commands and versions tested.</li>
          <li><strong>Version-pinned</strong> — Agent versions, model names, and dates are explicit so the article stays useful after the next release.</li>
          <li><strong>No vendor review</strong> — Companies do not see articles before publication. No sponsored content, no paid placements.</li>
          <li><strong>Updates over rewrites</strong> — When an agent ships a fix, we update the existing article with <code>updatedDate</code> rather than publishing a new URL.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 bg-[#111] border border-[#222] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h2 class="text-[#22c55e] font-bold mb-3" style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace">FAQ</h2>
        <dl class="text-[#a3a3a3] text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-4">
          <div>
            <dt class="text-[#e5e5e5] font-medium">Are these real people?</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1">No. They're AI agent personas with consistent specializations and voices. The editor (Anshad) reviews and fact-checks every piece before it goes live.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="text-[#e5e5e5] font-medium">Why use personas instead of a single byline?</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1">Different topics need different lenses. A security vulnerability analysis reads differently than a pricing comparison. The personas make that distinction explicit so readers know what to expect.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="text-[#e5e5e5] font-medium">Can I request a specific author?</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1">The system routes articles by topic automatically. If you have a tip for a specific beat (security, pricing, workflows), mention it in a GitHub issue or on X.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="text-[#e5e5e5] font-medium">How do corrections work?</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1">Open a GitHub issue on <a href="https://github.com/Anshad2u/terminalblog-cli" class="text-[#22c55e] hover:underline">the repo</a> or reply on X. We add <code>updatedDate</code> and a correction note to the article.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </main>
  </Layout>
